n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =3{b}_{3}-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =4{b}_{2}-5{b}_{1}, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & b & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351001 1113 #uuid "cebf33a6-1e88-5dcd-a020-6375d9d328e4" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351001 1145 "The coordinates of the vectors in $C$ relative to the basis $B$ are\n\n$$\n[{c}_{1}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{2}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{3}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3.$" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351003 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351004 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351005 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351006 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351007 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1041 "selection" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351003 13194139535473 true] [17592186351002 1110 #uuid "7953d339-0fdf-52f1-8dba-62f7b1861982" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351003 1034 "$a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535473 true] [17592186351003 1111 #uuid "eaa80bed-64be-5ebb-b39d-08253db29def" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351004 1034 "$a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=0$" 13194139535473 true] [17592186351004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319413